  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 215 PM MST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nTransitory ridging builds across the region into Wednesday, \nleading to dry conditions and warming temperatures, with latest \noperational and ensemble model continuing to indicate eastern \nPacific energy splitting as it translates across the \nIntermountain West Thursday and Friday, keeping the region in \nmoderate northwest flow into the end of the Thanksgiving Holiday\nweekend. This will keep chances of precipitation confined \nmainly to the Northern and Central Mtns, with temperatures \nremaining at and above seasonal levels. However, will need to \ncontinue to monitor the potential for surface high pressure \nbuilding across the Northern High Plains to send a backdoor cold\nfront into eastern Colorado later next weekend.",
